**Precedents, one per nation.** *Scotland:* Renewable Energy Generation Relief gives community-owned schemes (≥15% of annual profit to a community organisation) 100% relief up to £145k rateable value, tapering above. *England:* the Non-Domestic Rating (Renewable Energy Projects) Regulations 2013 let councils keep rates from designated renewable projects, protected from the April 2026 retention reset. *Wales:* onsite plant has been exempt since April 2024, so the roof half is [-already done.-]{+largely done (subject to the unchecked "onsite" reading in the ledger).+} For standalone hydro, the Welsh Government has run an application-based 100% rates relief for community hydro up to £50,000 rateable value. It was announced in 2018 and extended for 2019–20, with Ynni Ogwen named as a beneficiary ([R2](https://www.gov.wales/100-rates-relief-community-hydro-projects); [extension](https://www.gov.wales/100-business-rate-relief-continue-flow-community-hydro-projects)). Its status on the 2023 list is unconfirmed: guidance pages exist up to 2023–24, but those terms were not read (R3, cited in the ledger). *Spain:* municipalities may voluntarily waive up to **50% of IBI** (property tax) and **95% of ICIO** (works tax) on solar installs. Many do, so the lowest level gives up tax by choice, because the local return is worth more to it.
